  "_about": "M-style cluster after a photo of a current M8's cluster (design/photos/ref-m8-cluster.png): traced 1:1 off it (Nov 6 2026), then fitted to the X3's whole panel (heights stretched, side groups 1.2x; generated by design/gen_m.py, edit that): black, black cards with a thin grey rim whose top edge is the photo's curve, bowed glass rev blades (the photo's curve, 0..7000 rpm, the M40i's own scale) with a red marker block riding the rpm, the gear with its shifter programme (P, D3, S3, M3) and the speed in white over the centre line, four readout slots on the left where the M8 has its tyre block (boost, coolant, oil, intake by default; any sensor from the Readouts screen), the setup rows on the right (Eco Pro, Comfort, Sport, Sport Plus, Individual), the fuel and oil dials over the cards' lower corners, the drive mode under the speed. Backdrop, dials and the setup level bars are one shader (mdash); the rev bars are mtach: 3 effect layers plus the text sheets. Deviations from the photo, all forced by the X3: the badge is the M stripes without the M8 text; no range, clock or outside temperature of our own: the backdrop ends at y 660 so BMW's bottom strip shows them. Fuel and range from KombiIF statusRangeTankStatus (config.tankLitres is the full mark), outside temperature from EnvironmentalInformation. No speed limit sign: no app has found that signal yet. With 'Show Waze map inside the theme' the backdrop and blades swap for a map version (the same blades and numbers moved out to the sides) with a window between the numbers (content z 1 over the map's z 0), the gear, speed and mode in a row under it, and the readouts and setup rows stacked tighter on the narrower cards. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
